-- ADVERSARIAL PROBE for guard 2 of the M3 gate measurement. NOT corpus:
-- it lives under etc/ precisely so it is not swept up by jl4-test's
-- `examples/**` globs and does not need goldens.
--
-- The shape is the one that broke the first run of the measurement:
--
--     ((A AND C) OR B) AND D
--
-- an AND nested inside an OR nested inside an AND. `LSP.L4.Viz.Ladder` with
-- shouldSimplify=True distributes that into CNF, `(A OR B) AND (C OR B) AND D`,
-- which a lazy left-to-right walk costs at 3.125 questions -- while the emitted
-- docassemble interview keeps the SOURCE shape and really costs 2.875. The
-- error is one-directional (distribution can only ADD demands), so it inflated
-- the declaration-order baseline and flattered the planner.
--
-- § 227.503(a)(7) and § 227.503(a)(8) of jl4/examples/legal/regcf/denovo have
-- exactly this shape and are two of the eleven decisions the planner won on, so
-- the bug lived where the result lived. The first run's guard 2 could not catch
-- it: every interview it covered was a decision on which the two askers TIE.
--
-- Keep this probe in guard 2's case list. If a future change reintroduces a
-- normalising step between the source and the measured baseline, this is the
-- fixture that says so.
DECLARE Probe
    HAS
      @desc A
      `a` IS A BOOLEAN
      @desc B
      `b` IS A BOOLEAN
      @desc C
      `c` IS A BOOLEAN
      @desc D
      `d` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Whether the probe holds
GIVEN p IS A Probe @desc The probe subject
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `probe holds` p IF
        ((p's `a` AND p's `c`) OR p's `b`)
    AND p's `d`
